  "scope": "A positive seed A with orbit A t a palindrome beginning with pre forces every Agent124 certificate entry (pre, b) accepted by entryOK (any width k, any rank function with RowsClosed/ShortClosed) to satisfy t <= b + 1, and keeps pre out of every entry list passing the two premises of no_196_of_entries with base check N < t. Instances: seed 1186060307891929990 reaches its first palindrome (119 digits, prefix 4456) at t = 261, so 4456, 445 and 44 can never pass the t <= 100 route; 449 four-digit prefixes (and their three- and two-digit parents) with kernel-checked witnesses t > 100 (Over100); 1514 certified four-digit entries whose bound b + 1 is attained by a real seed (Sharp). Not claimed: anything about whether 196 is a Lychrel number; witnesses are lower bounds only, absence of a large witness does not make a prefix certifiable.",
